# AI Usage Log – Sprint 3

### Task 3.1: Establish the Unit Testing Strategy and Structure

**Purpose of AI Use:** Testing guidance and project organization

**Chat Link or Prompt/Response:** https://chatgpt.com/c/6af4cd61-efdc-83ea-b17b-df324be9c44b & https://chatgpt.com/c/6af4d618-93c0-83ea-be70-5795bfd3029b

**AI-Suggested Content:** AI helped determine how to organize the unit tests for Sprint 3 features and suggested using the existing Jest and Node.js testing frameworks. It explained where different tests should be placed and how to use a single command to execute the project's test suites. The suggested structure separated Jest tests into the `tests/` directory and Node.js built-in tests into the `test/` directory.

**Validation:** Reviewed the existing project structure, package configuration, and testing dependencies. Checked that the proposed locations were compatible with the existing test setup.

**Decision:** Accepted the suggested organization. Established `npm test` as the common command for running the project's automated tests and communicated the appropriate test directories to the team.

**Reflection:** AI helped establish a consistent testing structure for the team. This made it easier for team members to know where to place their tests and how to execute them without having to run different commands manually.

**Responsible Person:** Aminata


### Task 3.2: Develop Unit Tests for Application Analytics and Dashboard Functionality

**Purpose of AI Use:** Unit test development and implementation support

**Chat Link or Prompt/Response:** https://chatgpt.com/c/6afa6d56-7aa8-83ea-9574-d8320394c34d & https://chatgpt.com/c/6afa703e-6710-83ea-8c3a-f2207101c3d4

**AI-Suggested Content:** AI helped identify important functionality that needed to be tested for Sprint 3, including application information, application statuses, dashboard data, and the presentation of application information. It assisted in developing test cases and organizing the tests to verify the expected behavior of the application analytics functionality.

**Validation:** Reviewed the generated test cases against the existing application code and tested the functionality using the project's automated testing framework. Executed the tests to verify that the expected results matched the actual application behavior.

**Decision:** Accepted and modified the suggested test cases where necessary to match the existing implementation and project requirements.

**Reflection:** AI helped translate the application's functionality into individual test cases. It also helped identify different scenarios that needed to be considered when testing application information and dashboard functionality. However, the tests still needed to be executed and checked against the actual code.

**Responsible Person:** Aminata


